.TH ASTERCTL-UNSUBSCRIBE 1 "2026-10-06" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-unsubscribe \- remove an Event subscription
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B unsubscribe
.I SUBSCRIPTION_ID
.BI \-\-journal " PATH"
.BI \-\-client\-id " CLIENT_ID"
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove an Event subscription. Use the subscription ID returned by subscribe
or listed by subscriptions.
.PP
Require the owning stable client ID and its retained durable journal. Explicit
recovery precedes mutation; a fenced incarnation cannot change subscriptions.
.SH OUTPUT
Prints "Subscription removed" or "Subscription already absent" to stdout.
Both outcomes succeed.
.PP
With \-\-json, prints alreadyAbsent: false when removed, true when already absent.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Subscription removed or already absent.
.TP
.B 1
Command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Remove a subscription:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token unsubscribe "$SUBSCRIPTION_ID" \-\-journal ./publisher.redb \-\-client\-id chat-controller
.RE
.fi
.PP
Print the result as JSON:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token unsubscribe "$SUBSCRIPTION_ID" \-\-journal ./publisher.redb \-\-client\-id chat-controller \-\-json
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-subscribe (1),
.BR asterctl-subscriptions (1)
